{
  "title": "English flashcards",
  "back": "english/",
  "groups": [
    {"name": "Articles and Determiners", "cards": [
      ["a or an: ___ hour", "an (the h is silent, so it starts with a vowel sound)"],
      ["a or an: ___ university", "a (it starts with a \"yoo\" sound)"],
      ["a or an: ___ umbrella", "an"],
      ["Do rivers take \"the\"?", "Yes: the Ganga, the Yamuna"],
      ["Do sports take an article? He plays ___ cricket.", "No article: He plays cricket."],
      ["many or much: ___ books", "many (books can be counted)"],
      ["many or much: ___ water", "much (water can't be counted)"],
      ["few or a few: \"hardly any\"", "few. (A few means some.)"],
      ["Each and every are followed by a ___ noun", "singular: each boy, every girl"],
      ["some or any: I don't have ___ money.", "any (negative sentence)"]
    ]},
    {"name": "Nouns and Pronouns", "cards": [
      ["A group of sheep", "a flock"],
      ["A group of bees", "a swarm"],
      ["A group of wolves", "a pack"],
      ["A group of cows", "a herd"],
      ["A group of ships", "a fleet"],
      ["Plural of baby", "babies"],
      ["Plural of leaf", "leaves"],
      ["Plural of child", "children"],
      ["Plural of tooth", "teeth"],
      ["Plural of box", "boxes"],
      ["Plural of mouse", "mice"],
      ["Plural of sheep", "sheep (the same)"],
      ["Honesty is which kind of noun?", "abstract"],
      ["Gold is which kind of noun?", "material"],
      ["Delhi is which kind of noun?", "proper"],
      ["This pen is ___ (I).", "mine"],
      ["Object form of she", "her"],
      ["Belonging form of they, with no noun after it", "theirs"],
      ["Reflexive form of he", "himself"],
      ["its or it's: The dog wagged ___ tail.", "its (belonging). It's means it is."]
    ]},
    {"name": "Synonyms", "cards": [
